# Project Goal
The objective of this analysis is to determine which clusters of the covariate profiles of COVID-19 patients are associated with the presence of Post-COVID Condition (PCC) in the Respiratory Virus Transmission Network (RVTN) trial. 

# Methods

Descriptive analysis was conducted to provide an overall summary of our survey data. In details, we first explored the pattern of “unknown”, “prefer not to answer”, and missingness categories presented in the survey answers, and performed the pre-imputation processing on the data. Then we provided the summary of univariables, as well as the table of descriptive statistics by PCC status (Table 1). The remaining missing data is handled by single imputation with all the covariates and outcome. We evaluated covariate profiles and their risks using Bayesian profile regression (BPR) model [@molitor2010bayesian], odds ratio and credible interval for each profile was reported. We also compared the BPR model results with the results from the Latent Class Analysis (LCA) [@linzer2011polca] to validate our findings. All analyses were done using R version 4.3.2 along with PReMium, mice, and poLCA R packages.


The outcome was defined by the binary variable “any_symptom_fu90” to indicate if a patient experienced any symptoms at 90-day follow-up (i.e., has PCC presented). The list of symptoms considered are congestion/runny nose, sore throat, cough, shortness of breath, chest pain, diarrhea/constipation, weight loss, vomiting, fever, fatigue, dizziness, problems sleeping, change in mood, change in smell/taste, brain fog, headache, tingling, and increased fussiness/inconsolable crying.

Covariates of interest included: record type (Index case or Contact case), sex (Female, Male, Other binary/Transgender); race & ethnicity (Non-Hispanic White, Non-Hispanic Black, Non-Hispanic Other, Hispanic, Unknown); age group (< 18, 18-49, 50-64, 65+); presence of antiviral medication over 10 days (Yes, No, Unknown); hybrid vaccination & infection status (No vaccine and no prior infection, Vaccine only, Prior infection only, Both, Unknown); the indicator of experiencing any symptom over 10 days for fever, cough, sore throat, runny nose, congestion, fatigue, wheezing, shortness of breath, chest pain, loss of smell/taste, headache, abdominal pain, diarrhea, vomiting, and aches; smoking status (Yes, No), and underlying condition indicators for asthma, other lung disease, heart disease, diabetes, cancer, immunocompromising condition, obesity, kidney disease, liver disease, and immunesuppressing medications.

    
