The model outputs a risk matrix with a dimension of (5000, 5), where the number of rows equals the number of sweeps, and the number of columns is the number of clusters. Thus, the OR between two clusters can be calculated by: 1) computing the odds ratio of the risk within one sweep first, then take the average of the odds ratios across sweeps (denoted by “OR”), or 2) calculating the odds ratio of the averaged risks across sweeps (denoted by “OR_mean”). Both methods result in similar result, as shown in the Table 2.


```{r echo = F, results='asis',message=FALSE,warning=FALSE}
