# For binary variables, "profile" contains both risks for category 0 and category 1
# But we only want one risk for each binary variable in the radar plot, so need to extract the profile for either category 0 or 1, based on the definition of the variable.
# Here, for the first binary variable, I only want the risk for 0, so I force their nCategories to be only 1; 
# while for 6th to the last binary variables, I want the risk of 1, so I keep both categories and later only extract the second one using "profile[, meanSortIndex, j, 2]".
nCategories[1] = 1 # 1 
